arm64-darwin  a runtime call or record each compiler chooses (landing pads, guard aborts, __chkstk, atexit, a throw clang keeps where cxx1 calls terminate): emission, not spelling (tests/open/names-register.txt, "Emission, not names") - 2 names, e.g. <__Unwind_Resume <___cxa_guard_abort (r6n, names.sh on the Windows box beside clang 19.1.5, 2026-11-15)
x86_64-linux  a static local named by its function's symbol and its own, `f.n`, where clang writes _ZZ/_ZGVZ or ?$TSS (docs/CLAUDE-history.md, "A function-local static is named `f.n`, where Itanium writes `_ZZ1fvE1n`"); and a runtime call or record each compiler chooses (landing pads, guard aborts, __chkstk, atexit, a throw clang keeps where cxx1 calls terminate): emission, not spelling (tests/open/names-register.txt, "Emission, not names") - 7 names, e.g. <DW.ref.__gxx_personality_v0 <_Unwind_Resume (r6n, names.sh on the Windows box beside clang 19.1.5, 2026-11-15)
x86_64-windows  a static local named by its function's symbol and its own, `f.n`, where clang writes _ZZ/_ZGVZ or ?$TSS (docs/CLAUDE-history.md, "A function-local static is named `f.n`, where Itanium writes `_ZZ1fvE1n`"); and a runtime call or record each compiler chooses (landing pads, guard aborts, __chkstk, atexit, a throw clang keeps where cxx1 calls terminate): emission, not spelling (tests/open/names-register.txt, "Emission, not names") - 3 names, e.g. >?$TSS0@?1??f@@YAHXZ@4HA >?a@?1??f@@YAHXZ@4PAHA (r6n, names.sh on the Windows box beside clang 19.1.5, 2026-11-15)
